{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-009", "score": 0.126, "document": "# FAM:SF-CHT-009 | Study family SF-CHT-009: Superstar suppression by lineup and forced play type\n- observed_research_question: Superstar suppression by lineup and forced play type\n- auto_outcome_status: not a hypothesis test\n- observed_hypothesis: Named star initiators have identifiable lineup and forced-play-type suppressors in the possession graph.\n- observed_result: Jokic vs MIN lineup PPP 0.814, -0.385 (n=59); Curry vs HOU 0.851, -0.358 (n=47); Doncic vs LAC 0.733, -0.396 (n=30); Giannis forced PULL_UP 0.848, -0.540 vs preferred DRIVE (largest gap).\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE\n- observed_failure_evidence: No placebo or matching; later sequence work treated similar star-chain gaps as artifacts.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n>=30 for lineup cells cited\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_method: Jokic/Curry/Doncic/Giannis; min-15 gate on 8 play types; opposing DEFENSE_LINEUP ~84% coverage; 272-row CSV."}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-027", "score": 0.124, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-027 | Study family SF-APPS-027: Adaptation quality vs talent as predictor of series wins\n- observed_research_question: Adaptation quality vs talent as predictor of series wins\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: pct_ran_BEST - pct_ran_AVOID predicts series wins after controlling for RS net-rating talent.\n- observed_result: corr(talent, adapt)=+0.124. Per-series logistic: talent_diff_z +0.737 p=0.0213; adapt_diff_z +0.328 p=0.2755. Team-in-series cluster: talent p=0.0095, adapt p=0.2449. Univariate adapt beta=+0.311 p=0.1128. LPM: talent +0 [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:confounding\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:CONFOUNDING\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: After talent control adapt p=0.275; n~55 series cannot separate coaching adaptation from roster quality.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=55 series / 110 directions"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-076", "score": 0.094, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-076 | Study family SF-APPS-076: Trigger attribution: variance of H1->H2 PPP collapse\n- observed_research_question: Trigger attribution: variance of H1->H2 PPP collapse\n- auto_outcome_status: rejected\n- observed_hypothesis: Observable in-game process/usage/shot-selection/lineup/context changes explain suppression triggers beyond RTM.\n- observed_result: RTM (ppp_h1 alone) 32.9% of variance. Usage +0.0%; process+shot-zone +1.7%; lineup +0.0%; context +0.0%. Unexplained 65.4%. Total explained 34.6% (RTM=95% of explained).\n- auto_failure_mechanism: B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)\n- observed_failure_evidence: Process/usage/lineup/context add ~1.7 pp; residual 65.4% is idiosyncratic noise from small per-half n.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=40963 cells; 12617 triggers\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPS-070\n- observed_verdict: null\n- observed_failure_type: B_powered_null\n- auto_confidence: high (0.95)\n- auto_addresses_question: RQC:RQC-037"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-PAP-098", "score": 0.081, "document": "# FAM:SF-PAP-098 | Study family SF-PAP-098: Calibrated simulation vs Elo/net-rating/lineup+/- baselines\n- observed_research_question: Calibrated simulation vs Elo/net-rating/lineup+/- baselines\n- auto_outcome_status: not a hypothesis test\n- observed_hypothesis: The calibrated simulation beats simple team-level baselines on PPP MAE, win accuracy, log loss, and calibration error.\n- observed_result: VAL: CALIBRATION PPP MAE 0.1152 win 68.9% vs Elo 0.1154 / 69.4% and avg PPP 0.0928 / 67.9%; HOLDOUT: CALIBRATION PPP MAE 0.3369 win 54.8% logloss 0.778 vs Elo 0.3319 / 58.1% / 0.658 and lineup+/- win 64.5%\n- auto_failure_mechanism: C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)\n- observed_failure_evidence: holdout win accuracy 54.8% vs lineup+/- 64.5% and Elo 58.1%; val-to-holdout collapse 68.9%->54.8%\n- observed_sample_and_power: val ~193 games; holdout 155 games\n- auto_validation_status: same_pipeline_validation; evidence: PAP-098: 'validation ~193 games mid-jan-feb; holdout 155 games late-feb through'"}], "n_results": 4}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
